Package: qsm-pve-direct
Architecture: amd64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 dbus, ffmpeg, python3-aiortc, python3-av,
 pve-manager (>= 9), pve-manager (<< 10),
 qemu-server (>= 9), qemu-server (<< 10)
Description: WebRTC graphical console for Proxmox VE
 Streams QEMU D-Bus displays and optional LXC desktops to a browser using
 software or optional hardware video encoding, audio and interactive input.
 Existing Proxmox authentication and permissions authorize console access.
 .
 This package requires Proxmox VE, which is not part of Debian. It does not
 replace Proxmox packages. Install qsm-pve-direct-standalone for the stock-PVE
 signalling profile. LXC and the TCP gateway are separate optional packages.

Package: qsm-pve-direct-standalone
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, qsm-pve-direct (= ${binary:Version})
Description: standalone signalling profile for QSM Direct on stock Proxmox VE
 Enables the PVE-authorized HTTPS signalling service and guarded web-console
 integration. The initial free port starts at 18007 and is configurable.
 This profile requires official Proxmox VE packages; it does not supply them.

Package: qsm-pve-direct-gateway
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 qsm-pve-direct-standalone (= ${binary:Version}), adduser, systemd
Suggests: haproxy, coturn, nftables
Description: optional TCP 8006 relay gateway tools for QSM Direct
 Provides explicitly activated HTTPS and TURN/TCP multiplexing for a single
 Proxmox node behind a firewall or NAT forwarding only TCP 8006.
 Installation does not activate the gateway or its listeners.

Package: qsm-pve-direct-lxc
Architecture: all
Section: contrib/admin
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 qsm-pve-direct (= ${binary:Version}), pve-container (>= 6.1.13)
Description: host provisioning helper for QSM Direct LXC graphical consoles
 Configures a selected Debian or Ubuntu container for graphical console
 access from the Proxmox web interface. The matching guest package is built
 from the same source and embedded for installation inside the container.
 This helper belongs on the Proxmox host, not inside the container.

Package: qsm-console-guest
Architecture: all
Section: contrib/x11
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 sway, xwayland, python3-pyqt5, qtwayland5, acl, x11-xserver-utils,
 systemd, libpam-systemd, plasma-workspace, pulseaudio-utils, passwd
Recommends: kwin-wayland, plasma-workspace-wayland, kwin-x11,
 pipewire-pulse, wireplumber
Description: graphical console session inside an LXC container for QSM Direct
 Runs headless desktop sessions whose display and input are served through
 the host QSM media service. This package belongs inside a selected LXC
 container. It must not be installed on the Proxmox host.
